  "title": "The knot's spaces meet only through hubs",
  "subject": "Whether the knot's selected spaces (non-2-colourable cubic systems) can compose knot to knot, without a shared hub",
  "conclusion": "Across every nontrivial 3-edge cut of a knot's space the line side is exactly the knot (not-all-equal) and the point side exactly a hub (equality), and two sides that both accept knots can fail together only as complementary parity cosets. So the knot's spaces compose natively only through hubs, and a hub-free failing composition is a parity one.",
